  "id": "COMPOUND:27215 - PROTEIN:5787",
  "verbalization": "Bornyl chloride, (-)- is linked to RXF 631 through a series of molecular interactions, with SNU-387 acting as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that Bornyl chloride, (-)- targets SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Dendocarbin K, S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, and Tetraethylammonium. All of these compounds ultimately have RXF 631 as their target. This indicates a potential pathway where Bornyl chloride, (-)- may influence RXF 631 through SNU-387, possibly by modulating the activity of the compounds that interact with it. The consistent presence of SNU-387 as a common target across different compounds supports the idea of a shared mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 in mediating the effects of Bornyl chloride, (-)- on RXF 631, suggesting a possible role in cellular signaling or metabolic regulation.",
